WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:18.360
Hi, my name is Nico Cerioni. This is my Project 1 Video 2. This is a code behind my Coherent valuation application. Codex assisted with implementation and testing. The interface sends driver inputs to the engine through this run function, so the displayed valuation comes from the same financial model.

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:26.202
The deepcopy lab assumptions on line 91 and the lab project assumptions on line 98.

00:00:28.151 --> 00:00:39.151
Incredibly important. The engine imports a preserved lab model, it copies the assumptions, applies driver changes, and projects the statements. Copying the assumptions prevents a stress case from overwriting the base.

00:00:41.268 --> 00:00:43.268
Next on engine.py,

00:00:49.699 --> 00:01:10.699
There we go. Free cash flow to the firm starts with after-tax operating income, adds back noncash charges and subtracts working capital investment. Capital spending and intangible Purchases. Negative cash flow remains negative and reduces value. A separate calculation starts from operating cash flow and removes financing effects using after-tax interest and debt cost tax adjustment.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:28.304
The two calculations must agree under the model's current tax conventions, tax conventions. The check loop also tests statement reconciliation, the cash floor, and financing limits. Passing these checks establishes internal consistency, not forecast accuracy.

00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:33.218
This is the research Python script.

00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:49.559
The input components are on line 20 and the WACC calculations on line 26. The research file separates dated source inputs from judgments. Treasury yield and the equity risk premium are sourced. Beta, borrowing cost, and normalized tax are judgments.

00:01:49.559 --> 00:01:53.283
These produce a rounded WACC of 11.8%.

00:02:00.992 --> 00:02:10.992
Terminal reinvestment is on line 134. Terminal free cash flow to the firm on 135 and net claims at 144 to 145 and per share value at 149.

00:02:12.059 --> 00:02:17.059
Terminal growth is 3%. Terminal cash flow deducts reinvestment calculated as growth times.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:32.930
closing operating capital. The discount function values this cash flow using WACC minus growth and discounts it back. The equity bridge deducts debt, minority interest, finance leases, and pension deficits, and adds excess cash and investments.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:40.260
It retains $300 million of operating cash. Common equity is then divided by actual common shares.

00:02:43.213 --> 00:02:45.213
Moving on to the test engine.

00:02:46.408 --> 00:02:48.408
Let me scroll down.

00:02:50.732 --> 00:03:09.732
A high-risk claim is that the projected growth can be financed. This test increases growth by 5 percentage points in every forecast year, while holding other driver inputs constant. Faster growth requires inventory and capacity spending before cash is recovered. The test expects the scenario to fail its overall checks and specifically requires a cash-floor shortfall.

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:14.656
This prevents a conditional valuation from being treated as a fundable investment case.

00:03:16.447 --> 00:03:20.447
Down here, we have the integrated terminal and running this code.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.580
We see that it ran test one.

00:03:28.843 --> 00:03:46.843
Um, and it says okay in green, which means that it, it passed a check. The test passes because it detects the expected financial failure. It also checks rejection of invalid inputs and terminal growth equal to WACC. These are AI assisted integration tests separate from my historical changed input exercise.

00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:52.731
Next, we have the cold run.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:59.301
This includes six passing tests right here.

00:03:59.335 --> 00:04:02.335
lines 12 to 17.

00:04:02.532 --> 00:04:05.532
We can see that it ran the six tests.

00:04:06.062 --> 00:04:09.062
And that they were all passed.

00:04:09.764 --> 00:04:28.764
To reproduce from the repository, run python3 project1/test_engine.py. Then python3 project1/engine.py. The engine regenerates the saved model output. The clean run log records a fresh copy and virtual environment using only the standard library.

00:04:28.764 --> 00:04:34.338
All six tests pass and the base output was $75.60, which you can see right here.

00:04:41.431 --> 00:04:44.431
This is the dated Balance Sheet Proxies.

00:04:45.249 --> 00:05:01.249
The largest valuation risk is terminal dependence, about 87.4% of base enterprise value come from terminal value. The terminal reinvestment transition therefore matters substantially. Cash, debt, and shares also use disclosed dated proxies. While funding checks simplify maturity, timing and covenants.

00:05:02.127 --> 00:05:09.127
Passing tests support consistency and reproducibility. It does not prove the operating forecast or eliminate financing risks.

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:10.808
Thank you.
